---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Mayoral Tracker" description="Where the candidates for Denver Mayor stand on the issues, based on the public record." ogCategory="democracy">
  <section class="hero-mini">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 data-en="Mayoral Tracker" data-es="Rastreador de Alcalde">Mayoral Tracker</h1>
      <p data-en="The mayor proposes the budget, runs the police, and signs or vetoes every ordinance. This guide compiles what the public record tells us about each declared candidate for Denver Mayor - their positions, backgrounds, and track records." data-es="El alcalde propone el presupuesto, dirige la policía y firma o veta cada ordenanza. Esta guía recopila lo que el registro público nos dice sobre cada candidato declarado a alcalde - sus posiciones, antecedentes y trayectorias.">
        The mayor proposes the budget, runs the police, and signs or vetoes every ordinance. This guide compiles what the public record tells us about each declared candidate for Denver Mayor - their positions, backgrounds, and track records.
      </p>
      <p class="hero-sublink" data-en="Looking for City Council races? See the Council Candidate Tracker." data-es="&iquest;Buscas las carreras del Concejo Municipal? Consulta el Rastreador de Candidatos del Concejo.">
        Looking for City Council races? See the <a href="/tools/candidate-tracker">Council Candidate Tracker</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- Mayor's Race -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2 data-en="Mayor of Denver" data-es="Alcalde de Denver">Mayor of Denver</h2>
        <p data-en="Election: April 6, 2027. Runoff (if no candidate exceeds 50%): June 1, 2027. As of August 2026, at least ten candidates have declared; the field is not final until the December 16, 2026 filing deadline." data-es="Elección: 6 de abril de 2027. Segunda vuelta (si ningún candidato supera el 50%): 1 de junio de 2027. A partir de agosto de 2026, al menos diez candidatos se han declarado; la lista no es definitiva hasta la fecha límite de inscripción del 16 de diciembre de 2026.">
          Election: April 6, 2027. Runoff (if no candidate exceeds 50%): June 1, 2027. As of August 2026, at least ten candidates have declared; the field is not final until the December 16, 2026 filing deadline.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Mike Johnston -->
      <div class="candidate-card">
        <div class="candidate-header">
          <div class="candidate-info">
            <h3>Mike Johnston</h3>
            <span class="candidate-tag" data-en="Incumbent Mayor (2023-present)" data-es="Alcalde Titular (2023-presente)">Incumbent Mayor (2023&ndash;present)</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="candidate-context">
          <h4 data-en="What We Know From the Public Record" data-es="Lo Que Sabemos del Registro Público">What We Know From the Public Record</h4>
          <ul>
            <li data-en="Filed to run for reelection on August 10, 2026, entering an already crowded field of candidates hoping to unseat him. Elected mayor in 2023 runoff, defeating Kelly Brough by over 10 points. Former Colorado state senator (2013-2017) and education nonprofit executive." data-es="Se registró para la reelección el 10 de agosto de 2026, entrando en un campo ya numeroso de candidatos que esperan destituirlo. Elegido alcalde en segunda vuelta en 2023, derrotando a Kelly Brough por más de 10 puntos. Ex senador estatal de Colorado (2013-2017) y ejecutivo de organización sin fines de lucro educativa."><strong>Filed to run for reelection on August 10, 2026</strong>, entering an already crowded field of candidates hoping to unseat him. Elected mayor in 2023 runoff, defeating Kelly Brough by over 10 points. Former Colorado state senator (2013-2017) and education nonprofit executive.</li>
            <li data-en="Launched a hotel-based shelter initiative that the administration says achieved the 'largest reduction in street homelessness of any major American city.' Critics argue the model lacks wraparound services and long-term housing placements." data-es="Lanzó una iniciativa de refugios en hoteles que la administración dice logró la 'mayor reducción en la falta de vivienda en la calle de cualquier ciudad importante de Estados Unidos.' Los críticos argumentan que el modelo carece de servicios integrales y colocaciones de vivienda a largo plazo.">Launched a hotel-based shelter initiative that the administration says achieved the <strong>"largest reduction in street homelessness of any major American city."</strong> Critics argue the model lacks wraparound services and long-term housing placements.</li>
            <li data-en="Vetoed council's freezing-temperature encampment sweep moratorium. Bypassed City Council's 12-0 rejection of the Flock surveillance camera contract by structuring a deal under the $500K council approval threshold. Audit logs showed ICE searched Denver's camera data 1,400+ times." data-es="Vetó la moratoria del concejo sobre desalojos de campamentos durante temperaturas bajo cero. Evadió el rechazo 12-0 del Concejo Municipal del contrato de cámaras de vigilancia Flock estructurando un acuerdo por debajo del umbral de aprobación de $500K del concejo. Los registros de auditoría mostraron que ICE buscó los datos de las cámaras de Denver más de 1,400 veces."><strong>Vetoed</strong> council's freezing-temperature encampment sweep moratorium. <strong>Bypassed</strong> City Council's 12-0 rejection of the Flock surveillance camera contract by structuring a deal under the $500K council approval threshold. Audit logs showed ICE searched Denver's camera data 1,400+ times.</li>
            <li data-en="Laid off hundreds of city workers in 2025, citing budget shortfalls. Administration says it cut violent crime and auto theft in half during first term." data-es="Despidió a cientos de trabajadores municipales en 2025, citando déficit presupuestario. La administración dice que redujo el crimen violento y el robo de autos a la mitad durante el primer mandato.">Laid off hundreds of city workers in 2025, citing budget shortfalls. Administration says it <strong>cut violent crime and auto theft in half</strong> during first term.</li>
            <li data-en="Has supported STAR program funding. Denver voters approved municipal broadband in 2020; the city has not built it under Johnston's administration." data-es="Ha apoyado el financiamiento del programa STAR. Los votantes de Denver aprobaron la banda ancha municipal en 2020; la ciudad no la ha construido bajo la administración de Johnston.">Has supported STAR program funding. Denver voters approved municipal broadband in 2020; <strong>the city has not built it</strong> under Johnston's administration.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Lisa Calderón -->
      <div class="candidate-card">
        <div class="candidate-header">
          <div class="candidate-info">
            <h3>Lisa Calder&oacute;n</h3>
            <span class="candidate-tag" data-en="Justice Advocate, Executive Director of Women Uprising" data-es="Defensora de Justicia, Directora Ejecutiva de Women Uprising">Justice Advocate, Executive Director of Women Uprising</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="candidate-context">
          <h4 data-en="What We Know From the Public Record" data-es="Lo Que Sabemos del Registro Público">What We Know From the Public Record</h4>
          <ul>
            <li data-en="Third mayoral run. Finished third in 2023 with 18.21% of the vote - 3,200 votes and two points short of the runoff. Fourth-generation Denverite. Holds a bachelor's in English, master's in liberal studies, law degree, and doctorate in education." data-es="Tercera candidatura a la alcaldía. Terminó tercera en 2023 con el 18.21% de los votos - 3,200 votos y dos puntos por debajo de la segunda vuelta. Denverita de cuarta generación. Posee una licenciatura en inglés, maestría en estudios liberales, título de abogada y doctorado en educación.">Third mayoral run. Finished third in 2023 with 18.21% - 3,200 votes short of the runoff. Fourth-generation Denverite. Holds a <strong>bachelor's, master's, JD, and EdD</strong>.</li>
            <li data-en="Executive director of Women Uprising, which trains progressive women to run for office in Colorado. Teaches criminology at Regis University. Ran Denver's reentry program for people leaving incarceration." data-es="Directora ejecutiva de Women Uprising, que capacita a mujeres progresistas para postularse a cargos públicos en Colorado. Enseña criminología en la Universidad Regis. Dirigió el programa de reinserción de Denver para personas que salen de la cárcel.">Executive director of <strong>Women Uprising</strong>, which trains progressive women to run for office. Teaches criminology at Regis University. Ran Denver's <strong>reentry program</strong> for people leaving incarceration.</li>
            <li data-en="Housing: Build permanently affordable and social housing on city land and surplus buildings. Expand community land trusts and co-ops. Strengthen renter and homeowner protections. Accelerate ADUs and public housing, reform zoning. Shift to true housing-first with master leasing, wraparound services, building conversions, medical respite, and 24/7 STAR. Center people with lived experience." data-es="Vivienda: Construir vivienda permanentemente asequible y social en terrenos municipales y edificios excedentes. Expandir fideicomisos comunitarios de tierras y cooperativas. Fortalecer protecciones para inquilinos y propietarios. Acelerar ADUs y vivienda pública, reformar la zonificación. Cambiar a un verdadero enfoque de vivienda primero con contratos maestros, servicios integrales, conversión de edificios, respiro médico y STAR 24/7. Centrar a personas con experiencia vivida."><strong>Housing:</strong> Build permanently affordable and <strong>social housing</strong> on city land and surplus buildings. Expand <strong>community land trusts and co-ops</strong>. Strengthen renter/homeowner protections. Accelerate ADUs and reform zoning. Shift to true <strong>housing-first</strong> with master leasing, wraparound services, building conversions, medical respite, and <strong>24/7 STAR</strong>. Center people with lived experience.</li>
            <li data-en="Public Safety: Create a Department of Neighborhood Safety and expand STAR 24/7 citywide. Invest in violence interruption, restorative justice, and survivor services. Maintain public safety funding while increasing resources toward community-based prevention. Discontinue the Flock mass surveillance contract and implement alternative security, data control, and compliance solutions. Protect constitutional rights of all residents, including immigrants." data-es="Seguridad Pública: Crear un Departamento de Seguridad Vecinal y expandir STAR 24/7 en toda la ciudad. Invertir en interrupción de violencia, justicia restaurativa y servicios para sobrevivientes. Mantener el financiamiento de seguridad pública mientras se aumentan recursos hacia prevención comunitaria. Discontinuar el contrato de vigilancia masiva Flock e implementar alternativas de seguridad, control de datos y cumplimiento. Proteger los derechos constitucionales de todos los residentes, incluidos los inmigrantes."><strong>Public Safety:</strong> Create a <strong>Department of Neighborhood Safety</strong> and expand <strong>STAR 24/7 citywide</strong>. Invest in <strong>violence interruption, restorative justice, and survivor services</strong>. Maintain public safety funding while increasing community-based prevention. <strong>Discontinue the Flock mass surveillance contract</strong>. Protect constitutional rights of all residents, including immigrants.</li>
            <li data-en="Workers & Economy: Reinstate laid-off city workers and restore seniority protections. Support unions, livable wages, and Best Value Contracting. Replace the Career Service Board with worker-centered leadership. Expand city contracting for small, legacy, women- and minority-owned businesses, including at the airport. Provide tax holiday for burdened and new businesses. Oppose corporate giveaways and AI data center tax breaks." data-es="Trabajadores y Economía: Reincorporar a los trabajadores municipales despedidos y restaurar las protecciones de antigüedad. Apoyar sindicatos, salarios dignos y Contratación de Mejor Valor. Reemplazar la Junta de Servicio de Carrera con liderazgo centrado en los trabajadores. Expandir la contratación municipal para pequeñas empresas, empresas heredadas, y empresas de mujeres y minorías, incluyendo en el aeropuerto. Proporcionar vacaciones fiscales para negocios agobiados y nuevos. Oponerse a regalos corporativos y exenciones fiscales para centros de datos de IA."><strong>Workers &amp; Economy:</strong> <strong>Reinstate laid-off city workers</strong> and restore seniority protections. Support <strong>unions, livable wages, and Best Value Contracting</strong>. Replace the Career Service Board with worker-centered leadership. Expand city contracting for <strong>small, legacy, women- and minority-owned businesses</strong>. Oppose corporate giveaways and AI data center tax breaks.</li>
            <li data-en="Infrastructure & Climate: Build protected bike and pedestrian networks prioritizing community input. Advance Complete Streets and Vision Zero to prevent traffic deaths. Align transportation with climate goals and emissions reduction. Protect air and water quality and hold utilities accountable." data-es="Infraestructura y Clima: Construir redes protegidas de bicicletas y peatones priorizando la participación comunitaria. Avanzar Calles Completas y Visión Cero para prevenir muertes en el tránsito. Alinear el transporte con metas climáticas y reducción de emisiones. Proteger la calidad del aire y del agua y responsabilizar a las empresas de servicios públicos."><strong>Infrastructure &amp; Climate:</strong> Build protected bike and <strong>pedestrian networks</strong>. Advance <strong>Complete Streets and Vision Zero</strong> to prevent traffic deaths. Align transportation with climate goals. Protect air and water quality and hold utilities accountable.</li>
            <li data-en="Families & Cost of Living: Expand free universal childcare from birth to 5 years with wraparound support. Reduce healthcare costs through an affordable network of community-based providers. Invest in community-led food cooperatives and anti-hunger partners." data-es="Familias y Costo de Vida: Expandir el cuidado infantil universal gratuito desde el nacimiento hasta los 5 años con apoyo integral. Reducir costos de atención médica a través de una red asequible de proveedores comunitarios. Invertir en cooperativas alimentarias comunitarias y socios contra el hambre."><strong>Families &amp; Cost of Living:</strong> Expand free <strong>universal childcare birth to 5</strong> with wraparound support. Reduce healthcare costs through community-based providers. Invest in <strong>food cooperatives</strong> and anti-hunger partners.</li>
            <li data-en="Fiscal plan: Collect fair revenue from those who benefited most from Denver's growth. Secure long-term investments in housing and infrastructure through voter-approved social housing and mobility bonds. Prioritize prevention over reactive initiatives or vanity projects. Work with City Council to pass collaborative, moral and responsible budgets." data-es="Plan fiscal: Recaudar ingresos justos de quienes más se beneficiaron del crecimiento de Denver. Asegurar inversiones a largo plazo en vivienda e infraestructura a través de bonos de vivienda social y movilidad aprobados por los votantes. Priorizar la prevención sobre iniciativas reactivas o proyectos de vanidad. Trabajar con el Concejo Municipal para aprobar presupuestos colaborativos, morales y responsables."><strong>Fiscal plan:</strong> Collect fair revenue from those who benefited most from Denver's growth. Voter-approved <strong>social housing and mobility bonds</strong>. Prioritize prevention over reactive initiatives or vanity projects. Work with council on <strong>collaborative, moral and responsible budgets</strong>.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Aurelio Martinez -->
      <div class="candidate-card">
        <div class="candidate-header">
          <div class="candidate-info">
            <h3>Aurelio Martinez</h3>
            <span class="candidate-tag" data-en="Lifelong Five Points Resident, Former RNO President" data-es="Residente de Toda la Vida de Five Points, Ex Presidente de Organización Vecinal">Lifelong Five Points Resident, Former RNO President</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="candidate-context">
          <h4 data-en="What We Know From the Public Record" data-es="Lo Que Sabemos del Registro Público">What We Know From the Public Record</h4>
          <ul>
            <li data-en="Second mayoral run. Received 0.44% of the vote in 2023. Lifelong Denver resident, born and raised in Five Points / Curtis Park. Former president of the Curtis Park Block Council (neighborhood organization). Has kids, grandkids, and a great-grandchild in the neighborhood." data-es="Segunda candidatura a la alcaldía. Recibió el 0.44% de los votos en 2023. Residente de toda la vida de Denver, nacido y criado en Five Points / Curtis Park. Ex presidente del Curtis Park Block Council (organización vecinal). Tiene hijos, nietos y un bisnieto en el vecindario.">Second mayoral run. Received 0.44% in 2023. <strong>Lifelong Denver resident</strong>, born and raised in Five Points / Curtis Park. Former president of the <strong>Curtis Park Block Council</strong>. Has kids, grandkids, and a great-grandchild in the neighborhood.</li>
            <li data-en="Central issue is neighborhood preservation vs. overdevelopment. Says the city ignores residents, neighborhood organizations, and small businesses in favor of developers. Fought a PUD rezoning that allowed five- and seven-story buildings bordering the Curtis Park historic district. Says zoning laws should protect neighborhood character." data-es="Su tema central es la preservación de vecindarios frente al sobredesarrollo. Dice que la ciudad ignora a los residentes, las organizaciones vecinales y los pequeños negocios a favor de los desarrolladores. Luchó contra una rezonificación PUD que permitió edificios de cinco y siete pisos en los límites del distrito histórico de Curtis Park. Dice que las leyes de zonificación deben proteger el carácter del vecindario.">Central issue is <strong>neighborhood preservation vs. overdevelopment</strong>. Says the city ignores residents, neighborhood organizations, and small businesses in favor of developers. Fought a PUD rezoning allowing five- and seven-story buildings bordering the <strong>Curtis Park historic district</strong>.</li>
            <li data-en="Housing: Says Denver needs more housing for medium-income people, not luxury apartments. Wants city incentives tied to housing affordable for people making $45,000/year and below, not the current AMI-based definitions he says exclude working-class families. Opposes density increases in single-family-zoned neighborhoods. Supports preserving neighborhood zoning and parking." data-es="Vivienda: Dice que Denver necesita más vivienda para personas de ingresos medios, no apartamentos de lujo. Quiere incentivos municipales vinculados a vivienda asequible para personas que ganan $45,000/año o menos, no las definiciones actuales basadas en el AMI que dice excluyen a familias de clase trabajadora. Se opone a aumentos de densidad en vecindarios zonificados para viviendas unifamiliares. Apoya preservar la zonificación vecinal y el estacionamiento."><strong>Housing:</strong> Says Denver needs housing for medium-income people, not luxury apartments. Wants incentives tied to households making <strong>$45,000/year and below</strong>, not current AMI definitions. <strong>Opposes density increases</strong> in single-family-zoned neighborhoods. Supports preserving neighborhood zoning and parking.</li>
            <li data-en="Homelessness: Opposes both traditional shelter expansion and encampment sweeps. Proposed an 'Encampment Enforcement Team' to prevent tents from going up rather than clearing them after the fact. Favors assisted living-style housing over shelters. Says he would not arrest people under the urban camping ban. Would direct people to services and offer transportation." data-es="Personas sin hogar: Se opone tanto a la expansión tradicional de refugios como a los desalojos de campamentos. Propuso un 'Equipo de Aplicación de Campamentos' para prevenir que se instalen tiendas en lugar de desalojarlas después. Favorece vivienda estilo vida asistida sobre refugios. Dice que no arrestaría a personas bajo la prohibición de campamento urbano. Dirigiría a las personas a servicios y ofrecería transporte."><strong>Homelessness:</strong> Opposes both traditional shelter expansion and sweeps. Proposed an <strong>"Encampment Enforcement Team"</strong> to prevent tents from going up rather than clearing after the fact. Favors <strong>assisted living-style housing over shelters</strong>. Says he would <strong>not arrest</strong> people under the urban camping ban.</li>
            <li data-en="Wants to revitalize the 16th Street Mall and support small businesses, particularly in Capitol Hill and downtown. Says small businesses 'don't get any help from the city.' Goal is to make Denver 'the icon city of the United States' by centering neighborhoods, residents, and small businesses." data-es="Quiere revitalizar el 16th Street Mall y apoyar a los pequeños negocios, particularmente en Capitol Hill y el centro. Dice que los pequeños negocios 'no reciben ayuda de la ciudad.' Su meta es hacer de Denver 'la ciudad icónica de Estados Unidos' centrándose en vecindarios, residentes y pequeños negocios.">Wants to <strong>revitalize the 16th Street Mall</strong> and support small businesses. Says small businesses "don't get any help from the city." Goal: make Denver <strong>"the icon city of the United States"</strong> by centering neighborhoods, residents, and small businesses.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Robert Treta -->
      <div class="candidate-card">
        <div class="candidate-header">
          <div class="candidate-info">
            <h3>Robert Treta</h3>
            <span class="candidate-tag" data-en="Housing Developer, Unaffiliated" data-es="Desarrollador de Viviendas, No Afiliado">Housing Developer, Unaffiliated</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="candidate-context">
          <h4 data-en="What We Know From the Public Record" data-es="Lo Que Sabemos del Registro Público">What We Know From the Public Record</h4>
          <ul>
            <li data-en="Second mayoral run. Also ran in the 2023 race. Unaffiliated (former Democrat). Housing builder and developer with 30 years of experience in Denver. Also a short-term rental landlord in Denver and Mexico." data-es="Segunda candidatura a la alcaldía. También compitió en 2023. No afiliado (ex demócrata). Constructor y desarrollador de viviendas con 30 años de experiencia en Denver. También propietario de alquileres a corto plazo en Denver y México.">Second mayoral run. Also ran in the 2023 race. <strong>Unaffiliated</strong> (former Democrat). Housing builder and developer with <strong>30 years of experience</strong> in Denver. Also a short-term rental landlord in Denver and Mexico.</li>
            <li data-en="Central issue is government corruption and nonprofit accountability. Says city funnels tens of millions in sales tax revenue to politically connected nonprofits like Caring for Denver with 'no accountability, no oversight by the city auditor.' Wants to audit these funding streams." data-es="Su tema central es la corrupción gubernamental y la rendición de cuentas de las organizaciones sin fines de lucro. Dice que la ciudad canaliza decenas de millones en ingresos de impuestos de ventas a organizaciones sin fines de lucro políticamente conectadas como Caring for Denver con 'sin rendición de cuentas, sin supervisión del auditor de la ciudad.' Quiere auditar estos flujos de financiamiento.">Central issue is <strong>government corruption and nonprofit accountability</strong>. Says city funnels tens of millions in sales tax revenue to politically connected nonprofits like Caring for Denver with "no accountability, no oversight by the city auditor."</li>
            <li data-en="Housing platform focuses on deregulation. Says Denver building permits take up to 14 months vs. one day in Lincoln County. Argues regulations add 25-35% to housing costs in Denver, approximately $150,000-$200,000 per build. Wants to reduce permitting times and regulatory burden to lower housing costs." data-es="La plataforma de vivienda se enfoca en la desregulación. Dice que los permisos de construcción en Denver toman hasta 14 meses vs. un día en el Condado de Lincoln. Argumenta que las regulaciones agregan 25-35% a los costos de vivienda en Denver, aproximadamente $150,000-$200,000 por construcción. Quiere reducir los tiempos de permisos y la carga regulatoria para bajar los costos de vivienda."><strong>Housing platform focuses on deregulation.</strong> Says Denver building permits take up to 14 months vs. one day in Lincoln County. Argues regulations add 25-35% to housing costs (~$150,000-$200,000 per build). Wants to reduce permitting times and regulatory burden.</li>
            <li data-en="Critical of out-of-state donor influence in Denver politics, specifically naming Michael Bloomberg and Reid Hoffman. Critical of local media, particularly Nine News. Has expressed interest in America PAC and Elon Musk involvement in Colorado local elections." data-es="Crítico de la influencia de donantes de fuera del estado en la política de Denver, nombrando específicamente a Michael Bloomberg y Reid Hoffman. Crítico de los medios locales, particularmente Nine News. Ha expresado interés en la participación de America PAC y Elon Musk en las elecciones locales de Colorado.">Critical of <strong>out-of-state donor influence</strong> in Denver politics, naming Michael Bloomberg and Reid Hoffman. Critical of local media. Has expressed interest in <strong>America PAC and Elon Musk</strong> involvement in Colorado local elections.</li>
            <li data-en="Also identifies unchecked short-term rental conversions (circa 2015) as a factor in Denver's housing crisis, saying investors converting rental properties to Airbnbs removed significant inventory before regulation was written. Describes himself as a 'results guy' focused on hands-on housing expertise." data-es="También identifica las conversiones sin control de alquileres a corto plazo (circa 2015) como un factor en la crisis de vivienda de Denver, diciendo que los inversores que convirtieron propiedades de alquiler a Airbnbs eliminaron un inventario significativo antes de que se escribiera la regulación. Se describe como un 'tipo de resultados' enfocado en experiencia práctica en vivienda.">Also identifies <strong>unchecked short-term rental conversions</strong> (circa 2015) as a factor in Denver's housing crisis - says investors converting rentals to Airbnbs removed significant inventory before regulation was written. Describes himself as a "results guy" focused on hands-on housing expertise.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Shontel Lewis -->
      <div class="candidate-card">
        <div class="candidate-header">
          <div class="candidate-info">
            <h3>Shontel Lewis</h3>
            <span class="candidate-tag" data-en="District 8 Council Member · Former RTD Board Member" data-es="Concejala del Distrito 8 · Ex Miembro de la Junta de RTD">District 8 Council Member · Former RTD Board Member</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="candidate-context">
          <h4 data-en="What We Know From the Public Record" data-es="Lo Que Sabemos del Registro Público">What We Know From the Public Record</h4>
          <ul>
            <li data-en="Filed to run for Mayor on July 16, 2026, choosing not to seek re-election to her District 8 council seat (see the Candidate Tracker for that now-open race). Elected District 8 council member in the June 2023 runoff; born and raised in Denver's historic Five Points neighborhood." data-es="Se registró para la Alcaldía el 16 de julio de 2026, optando por no buscar la reelección a su escaño del Distrito 8 (vea el Rastreador de Candidatos para esa contienda ahora abierta). Elegida concejala del Distrito 8 en la segunda vuelta de junio de 2023; nacida y criada en el histórico vecindario Five Points de Denver."><strong>Filed to run for Mayor on July 16, 2026</strong>, choosing not to seek re-election to her District 8 council seat (see the <a href="/tools/candidate-tracker">Candidate Tracker</a> for that now-open race). Elected District 8 council member in the June 2023 runoff; born and raised in Denver's historic Five Points neighborhood.</li>
            <li data-en="Served on the Regional Transportation District (RTD) Board of Directors from 2019 to 2022, chairing the Performance Committee. Previously Vice President of Equity, Inclusion and Diversity at the Colorado Coalition for the Homeless and Director of Engagement and Strategy at Denver Public Schools." data-es="Sirvió en la Junta Directiva del Distrito de Transporte Regional (RTD) de 2019 a 2022, presidiendo el Comité de Rendimiento. Anteriormente Vicepresidenta de Equidad, Inclusión y Diversidad en la Coalición de Colorado para Personas sin Hogar y Directora de Compromiso y Estrategia en las Escuelas Públicas de Denver.">Served on the <strong>RTD Board of Directors</strong> from 2019 to 2022, chairing the Performance Committee. Previously VP of Equity at the Colorado Coalition for the Homeless and Director of Engagement and Strategy at Denver Public Schools.</li>
            <li data-en="On council, identified as part of the progressive bloc; named social housing a top 2025 priority. Advocated for housing-first policies and tenant protections, and supported the council effort to secure nearly $30 million in rental assistance in the 2024 budget." data-es="En el concejo, se identificó como parte del bloque progresista; nombró la vivienda social como prioridad principal para 2025. Abogó por políticas de vivienda primero y protecciones para inquilinos, y apoyó el esfuerzo del concejo para asegurar casi $30 millones en asistencia de alquiler en el presupuesto de 2024.">On council, identified as part of the <strong>progressive bloc</strong>; named social housing a top 2025 priority. Advocated for housing-first policies and tenant protections, and supported the council effort to secure nearly $30 million in rental assistance in the 2024 budget.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Additional declared candidates -->
      <div class="candidate-card">
        <div class="candidate-header">
          <div class="candidate-info">
            <h3 data-en="Other declared candidates" data-es="Otros candidatos declarados">Other declared candidates</h3>
            <span class="candidate-tag" data-en="Filed with the Denver Elections Division" data-es="Registrados ante la División de Elecciones de Denver">Filed with the Denver Elections Division</span>
          </div>
